HexaShell
An agent harness for robot manipulation: RoboDojo's two-arm table tasks, RoboCasa365, LIBERO-PRO,
RoboTwin 2.0, and a real robot through URAI.

HexaShell's code is its own, but it rests on other projects' files, measurements and ideas:

RoboDojo (MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 RoboDojo Contributors)
  - hexashell/assets/X5A.urdf is a copy of the ARX X5 robot description in RoboDojo's assets.
  - hexashell/assets/robot_model.npz holds triangles derived from RoboDojo's ARX X5 meshes
    (made by bench/build_robot_points.py).
  - xpolicylab/HexaShell follows the layout of RoboDojo's XPolicyLab policy template.
  - scripts/patches/robodojo-layout-ids.patch changes RoboDojo's env/seed_manager/seed_manager.py
    so that ROBODOJO_LAYOUT_IDS selects the layouts of an evaluation (used by scripts/run_one.sh
    and scripts/batch.sh; RoboDojo's own evaluation runs without it).

RoboProbe (Apache License 2.0)
  - prompts/ladders/*.md are RoboDojo's task descriptions and scoring tables, copied unchanged
    from RoboProbe; see prompts/ladders/README.md and prompts/ladders/LICENSE.

PyRUA-Lean (Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2026 PyRUA-Lean Contributors)
  Several facts about the simulator and several design ideas were first worked out there:
  - simulator facts: the arm-base poses (re-checked against our own recordings with
    bench/fit_bases.py), the joint ranges the simulator lets the arms reach, the grasp-point and
    fingertip offsets along link6, the squeezed-gripper width fit, the wrist-camera mount, the
    head-camera pose and both focal lengths;
  - motion constants: at most 0.15 rad per joint per action, up to 8 actions to settle, arrival
    within 1 cm / 5 degrees, near misses accepted within 2 cm / 8 degrees, lifting before
    swinging home;
  - ideas: the model works the robot by writing Python cells against a robot object; objects are
    measured in 3-D from several RGB cameras as the shape that agrees with all their outlines,
    with the robot's own pixels left out and measured heights remembered; a bowl's reading from
    its rim, kept only where it explains the views clearly better; with one camera, the height
    read from how far the outline's upright sides reach out on the table plane;
  - prompt advice adopted after comparing our prompt with a port of PyRUA-Lean's: coming down onto
    an upright object from above for a level side grasp, measuring every object before the arms
    move, judging a pour by what is left when the container turns back up, homing before a
    benchmark-driven arm's turn, that a bumped container moves, switching arms or reaching with a
    tilted or level hand when one arm cannot reach, that the way a task is done can be checked,
    and measuring a low object from the top grasp's approach pose; skills/robodojo/hang_mugs.md's level
    body grasp and level slide onto the peg were seen in a run with that port.

HexaShell-Preview (HexaShell 1.0; this repository's earlier version, branch v1.0:
  https://github.com/HexaFuture/HexaShell/tree/v1.0)
  - ideas carried over: dry-run reachability checks, two-view triangulation with a ray-gap check,
    ray-plane intersection at a given height, a mesh-based robot mask, support-height
    detection, and the hover advice for re-measuring from above.

RoboCasa365 and robosuite (MIT License)
  - hexashell/benches/robocasa runs RoboCasa's kitchens, tasks and success checks unchanged,
    through robosuite's official controllers; the 50 tasks, their sets and step limits are
    RoboCasa365's benchmark split.  Both are included only as git submodules
    (third_party/robocasa, third_party/robosuite) at upstream commits, with the changes to
    RoboCasa listed in THIRD_PARTY_VERSIONS.md applied by scripts/patch_third_party.py;
    RoboCasa's assets are not included.

LIBERO and LIBERO-PRO (MIT License)
  - hexashell/benches/libero runs LIBERO-PRO's suites through LIBERO's own environments,
    controller and goal checks (the rpent-libero and rpent-liberopro packages); neither is part
    of this repository;
  - the step limits of the test (OFFICIAL_STEPS of hexashell/benches/libero/protocol.py) and its
    10 settling steps are those of LIBERO-PRO's own evaluation.

RoboTwin 2.0 (MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 Tianxing Chen)
  - hexashell/assets/robotwin_aloha_arms.urdf holds the joints of the two front arms of RoboTwin's
    aloha-agilex robot, copied from its assets (embodiments/aloha-agilex/urdf/
    arx5_description_isaac.urdf; meshes, inertia and the rest of the robot left out);
  - hexashell/benches/robotwin runs RoboTwin's tasks, controller, ray-traced cameras and success
    checks unchanged, through the rlinf-robotwin-runtime package (MIT); neither is part of this
    repository;
  - STEP_LIMITS of hexashell/benches/robotwin/protocol.py are RoboTwin's step limits
    (_eval_step_limit.yml), and the test takes its seeds and instructions as RoboTwin's evaluation
    does (scripts/eval_policy.sh: the first seeds from 100000 its expert solves; for demo_randomized,
    instructions from the tasks' 'unseen' description templates).

RPent (Apache License 2.0)
  - hexashell/benches/robotwin/eval_seeds.json is a copy of RPent's RoboTwin evaluation list
    (robots/robotwin/eval/demo_randomized.json at commit 886b3b2: 50 tasks, five checked seeds
    each, with their instructions), which gives the task list and a check of the seed scan.

URAI (Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2026 Hexafuture Inc. and the URAI authors,
  https://github.com/HexaFuture/URAI)
  - hexashell/real/urai/capsules.py is a copy of the ray-capsule intersection and its pixel windows
    from URAI's urai/robot/scene.py (Capsule, _capsule_hit, _capsule_window, _camera_rays,
    _pixel_rays, _window), with public names and without the capsules' colour;
  - prompts/urai/*.md are the English real-robot prompts of URAI's HexaShell harness, copied
    unchanged, and the sentences of hexashell/real/urai/texts.py are that harness's English ones;
  - hexashell/real/urai follows that harness and talks to URAI only over its HTTP interface; URAI
    itself is not part of this repository.

SAM3 (Meta) runs as a separate local service (services/sam3_server.py); its code and weights are
not part of this repository.
